 le-y: 100%\; --skew-x: 0deg\; --skew-y: 0deg\; --origin-x: 50%\; --origin-
 y: 50%\; opacity: var(--opacity\, 1)\; transform: translateX(var(--transla
 te-x)) translateY(var(--translate-y)) rotate(var(--rotation)) scale(var(--
 scale-x)\, var(--scale-y)) skewX(var(--skew-x)) skewY(var(--skew-y))\; tra
 nsform-origin: var(--origin-x) var(--origin-y)\; } Join us for an inspirin
 g afternoon at the Petaluma Arts Center for Teaching As Art Practice \, a 
 panel discussion exploring the dynamic relationship between teaching and c
 reative practice. Drawing from Aristotle’s quote\, “Those who can\, do
 \; those who understand\, teach\,” this conversation brings together art
 ist educators from across the North Bay to discuss how teaching art shapes
 \, challenges\, and enriches their own artistic work. Through personal exp
 eriences and shared perspectives\, panelists will reflect on mentorship\, 
 creative process\, pedagogy\, and the evolving role of educators within co
 ntemporary art communities. The panel features professors and teachers fro
 m Sonoma State University\, College of Marin\, and Santa Rosa Junior Colle
 ge. Moderated by New Voices Curator Emma Logan \, this engaging discussion
  offers insight into the intersection of artmaking\, education\, and commu
 nity connection. #block-yui_3_17_2_1_1781805721920_3884 { } #block-yui_3_1
